f31b0af6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-7-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":7,"verse":12,"english":"The dominion of Death is like the mighty main, having his rod for aquatic animals, agonies for the frees that cover its islands, the noose for the billows, his attendants for the serpents and his terrible fever for the dreadful attitude of the deep. And diving into this terrible deep, you did, O king, discomfit Death himself and win glorious victory. And every one was pleased there with your successful fight.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.71,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-7-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6007012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ac6cac5d6eff0c01f2c5ce383ef28862281a0a763b5ef5a76c7b506ed7bcbe0f","compact":"5241ecf4f50fffe8ca60be4467225aac6ad9350d23d85f578d2268cabd68bb69","nasal":"46bed50b048b92452f882731ed8af556c3ee6ec07db1eab7044e53c5ccf5728c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-7-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":7,"verse":13,"english":"The dominion of Death is like the mighty main, having his rod for aquatic animals, agonies for the frees that cover its islands, the noose for the billows, his attendants for the serpents and his terrible fever for the dreadful attitude of the deep. And diving into this terrible deep, you did, O king, discomfit Death himself and win glorious victory. And every one was pleased there with your successful fight.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-7-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6007013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"11bebe151b2d4a0ae88d4d78a9c6a46f8de113cc20fbe9be95b07117c1c124e3","compact":"d65e1f8fbc01c2383bc30f71ff9f3ea24e0058d907bae6ee6b1ab76c45fe8367","nasal":"d65e1f8fbc01c2383bc30f71ff9f3ea24e0058d907bae6ee6b1ab76c45fe8367"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-7-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":7,"verse":14,"english":"The Earth was filled with various heroic Kșatriyas, resembling Sakra in prowess as she is adorned now with various trees.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-7-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6007014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"33cbcbcdf101049f865e496e70bfe2771387c64dfeda0649e2f10a3e5185244f","compact":"eab0df27ace849b2a3df3d60f5e6394840243a7bfebc560f492da1692fd0e727","nasal":"eab0df27ace849b2a3df3d60f5e6394840243a7bfebc560f492da1692fd0e727"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-7-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":7,"verse":15,"english":"Rāghava is not their equal either is strength or prowess. And all those heroes, hard to repress in battle, were slain by you, O king.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-7-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6007015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"76c6e5d1b1189d5438d882d9df12bf90ca550ab89f1f4bd24222aa4e68078526","compact":"3c2030412c0f028adff9b21a38b743ffebf9d16a2ab1f7f70c68243d2454e8a6","nasal":"3c2030412c0f028adff9b21a38b743ffebf9d16a2ab1f7f70c68243d2454e8a6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-7-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":7,"verse":16,"english":"O king, you must not think that this calamity, coming from an ignoble person is not insignificant. You shall slay Rāghava.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-7-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6007016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3ee7048d220e90bf2de5b71d8430e27e21dafb9a71a6f0973f2b1b4509ff0009","compact":"fbcc64c8d2924150e3016ad36185e2cf94876339ef14ce45791957df52c51935","nasal":"6046b3